e` name resolution\n- a3c6140 - docs(builtins:array): Update edge cases table\n- c9f5b19 - test(builtins:array): Update empty array expectations\n- e876a9d - test(utils): Cover function name resolution\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Ryuu Mitsuki <dhefam31@proton.me>","tree":{"sha":"cd384a4424d913836f5a49cbca3f70c32126d71f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitsuki31/tguard-js/git/trees/cd384a4424d913836f5a49cbca3f70c32126d71f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitsuki31/tguard-js/git/commits/d056de0eb3d9106fc215f27f67da76d19735fdc5","verification":{"payload":"tree cd384a4424d913836f5a49cbca3f70c32126d71f\nparent bb82ee5ea63a693f56370af3d5a17257a349dc0f\nparent e876a9d80dd685bcc76d05eb2af4394c1503e023\nauthor Ryuu Mitsuki <dhefam31@proton.me> 1778204454 +0700\ncommitter Ryuu Mitsuki <dhefam31@proton.me> 1778204721 +0700\n\nfix: Correct `getType()` and array guard edge cases (#1)\n\nThis PR improves runtime type introspection behavior for `getType()`,\nrefines array guard semantics for empty arrays, and expands test\ncoverage for edge cases across utility and array modules.\n\nThe changes primarily focus on improving consistency, developer\nexperience, and runtime correctness across Node.js and modern JavaScript\nruntimes while preserving Node.js v14 compatibility.\n\n---\n\n- adf92f1 - fix(utils): Improve `getType` name resolution\n- a3c6140 - docs(builtins:array): Update edge cases table\n- c9f5b19 - test(builtins:array): Update empty array expectations\n- e876a9d - test(utils): Cover function name resolution\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: Ryuu Mitsuki <dhefam31@proton.me>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEm92tubt+kYpkGEDs6coHz6zDdJoFAmn9QDEACgkQ6coHz6zD\ndJr/uA/+LWxfr/vEom4HsXG4NEolZI8jmr06pa4D+JUm+9CePlHsCpjj+/cNXUM6\nD6XFAk+eSmV/xI2CJtmHZoVbq9xZhPHcU7amJh+ZlPEC2GLhU4qN1CM3YPPJggjf\nfaa4pnv7ociLgHc4GTCcy2mSQA8cY8o2DVSPBmpy3MQ/XN12dt1nfy/i56T3nDmn\nuaCbAA7UPcPW4iiNibwUcNfsiJIPELPyGGnV5ZWgPbecq52VdYKLy/vGdcRxf3Q1\n0gmGPU0Nah0