"sha":"c253bd7425bebacc886df943645ffdd530c29af4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kekcoke/civichealth/commits/c253bd7425bebacc886df943645ffdd530c29af4"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/kekcoke/civichealth/commit/ca245f43d065f0c0e825b8be3df862dacadea415","sha":"ca245f43d065f0c0e825b8be3df862dacadea415","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kekcoke/civichealth/commits/ca245f43d065f0c0e825b8be3df862dacadea415"}],"sha":"db586e8b8d24b12f6785e6c22c0afa140f918843","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kekcoke/civichealth/commits/db586e8b8d24b12f6785e6c22c0afa140f918843"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25495857?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kekcoke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kekcoke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kekcoke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kekcoke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kekcoke","id":25495857,"login":"kekcoke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NDk1ODU3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kekcoke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kekcoke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kekcoke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kekcoke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kekcoke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kekcoke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kekcoke/civichealth/commits/ca245f43d065f0c0e825b8be3df862dacadea415/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T20:26:53Z","email":"kolioane@gmail.com","name":"Kevin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T20:26:53Z","email":"kolioane@gmail.com","name":"Kevin"},"message":"feat(phase-3): Secure Health Integration — networking, ha-clinical remote, PHI middleware\n\nHybrid Networking:\n- infra/networking/cors-policy.md: CORS rules, Nginx DMZ reverse-proxy\n  config, VPN/ExpressRoute topology diagram, security constraints\n\nHA BFF — PHI Enforcement Layer:\n- middleware/phi_sanitizer.rb: Rack middleware (defence-in-depth) that\n  scrubs PHI fields from GraphQL responses for non-ha_clinician callers\n  (HIPAA / RA 10173 compliant); applied globally via `use` in app.rb\n- lib/audit_logger.rb: Compliance audit logger for clinical data access;\n  mirrors SQL Server audit_clinical_access trigger; ships to SIEM/Azure Monitor\n- app.rb: Wired PhiSanitizer middleware and AuditLogger require\n\nha-clinical Angular Remote (Private Cloud MFE):\n- package.json: Angular 17 + Apollo Angular + Module Federation deps\n- webpack.config.js: Module Federation config exposing ClinicalModule\n  and HealthStatusElement to Portal Shell host\n- clinical.module.ts: ClinicalModule with child routes for patient\n  record, appointments, encounters, prescriptions\n- clinical-dashboard.component.ts: Dashboard with listAppointments +\n  searchProviders GraphQL queries\n- patient-record.component.ts: Full EMR view via getPatientRecord query\n- appointments.component.ts: scheduleAppointment + cancelAppointment mutations\n- encounters.component.ts: listEncounters + createEncounter\n- prescriptions.component.ts: getActivePrescriptions query\n- environments/: Dev (localhost) and prod (ha-proxy.internal) configs\n\nHealth Status Web Component (Partial Integration Adapter):\n- health-status.element.ts: Framework-agnostic Custom Element\n  <health-status-widget> embedded in LGU React portal; shows appointment\n  count and next appointment date only — zero PHI exposed to citizens\n\nCo-Authored-By: AdaL <adal@sylph.ai>","tree":{"sha":"acce0e7e2cde43c191dde9a4cb998bb42925c08d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kekcoke/civichealth/git/trees/acce0e7e2cde43c191dde9a4cb998bb42925c08d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kekcoke/civichealth/git/commits/ca245f43d065f0c0e825b8be3df862dacadea415","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsi