://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/55e71ca8b8c97e2f5d6f39d5e9759b20e7941af0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T13:17:37Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T13:17:37Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"message":"The OTA job fetches the EAS CLI, because CI has no global one\n\nThe first run with a real token got as far as publishing and died on\n`Command \"eas\" not found`. `pnpm exec eas` resolves on the owner''s machine\nbecause eas-cli is installed globally there; it is not a dependency of this\nrepo, so a clean CI install has nothing to exec.\n\nPinned rather than latest, so a release of the CLI cannot change what this job\ndoes without somebody choosing it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014nCiMWkWZJQ6zqSLRLtKtz","tree":{"sha":"8200a6608a59abbc82d71d3758b98b09316195cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/trees/8200a6608a59abbc82d71d3758b98b09316195cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/commits/55e71ca8b8c97e2f5d6f39d5e9759b20e7941af0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/fo