ithub.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/bb7e0c7cc348a3bf26de8eb95d04e71135978e39"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/45ef9248c95fc17241089acb68bcba1db07df10c","sha":"45ef9248c95fc17241089acb68bcba1db07df10c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/45ef9248c95fc17241089acb68bcba1db07df10c"}],"sha":"8e1f7dfa6f9e45fb0866f478529e3bd5385ed2d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/8e1f7dfa6f9e45fb0866f478529e3bd5385ed2d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Layott","id":90828865,"login":"Layott","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODI4ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/45ef9248c95fc17241089acb68bcba1db07df10c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T10:20:47Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T10:20:47Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"message":"Build releases on EAS, and give the website that same artifact\n\nOwner''s rule, 19 August 2026: whatever is on EAS is what the site hands out.\nThe same file, not the same commit. Two builds of one commit are two different\nbinaries, and a bug report against \"the download\" has to mean exactly one\nthing.\n\n`pnpm release:android` is the whole release now. It builds on EAS, waits,\ndownloads the finished artifact, renames it from the version, build number and\ncommit EAS recorded for that build rather than from the working tree, publishes\nthat file to the website, and pushes the matching OTA on the same channel. The\nEAS build id and artifact URL go into the release row''s notes, so a download\ncan be traced back to the build that produced it.\n\nTwo things that would have bitten on the first run:\n\nThe build counters do not agree. build-apk-local.ps1 numbers builds by commit\ncount and has reached 229; EAS keeps its own and starts at 1. The site hands\nout the highest build number, so a lower one would be invisible, and Android\nrefuses to install a lower versionCode over a copy already on a phone, which\nshows up as \"app not installed\" with no reason given. publish-apk.mjs now reads\nthe current highest and refuses rather than publishing something nobody can\ninstall. The one-time fix is `eas build:version:set`, which the runbook says.\n\n`autoIncrement` was only on the production profile, so every preview build\nwould have carried the same versionCode as the last one.\n\nThe local script keeps its place for putting something on a phone to look at,\nand its header now says it is not a release. It is also still the only way to\nbuild without EAS quota, since `eas build --local` refuses to run on Windows.\n\nUntested end to end: the machine is not signed in to EAS, so the build, the\ndownload and the publish have not been run. Syntax and the JSON are checked.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JEPvbznPoLupeJmcBrdvod","tree":{"sha":"ed8fa76bf9fca4217b9a5332152768f15143ecb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/trees/ed8fa76bf9fca4217b9a5332152768f15143ecb8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/commits/45ef9248c95fc17241089acb68bcba1db07df10c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Layott","id":90828865,"login":"Layott","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODI4ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/45ef9248c95fc17241089acb68bcba1db07df10c","node_id":"C_kwDOSVUfFtoAKDQ1ZWY5MjQ4Yzk1ZmMxNzI0MTA4OWFjYjY4YmNiYTFkYjA3ZGYxMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/bb7e0c7cc348a3bf26de8eb95d04e71135978e39","sha":"bb7e0c7cc348a3bf26de8eb95d04e71135978e39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/bb7e0c7cc348a3bf26de8eb95d04e71135978e39"}],"sha":"45ef9248c95fc17241089acb68bcba1db07df10c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/45ef9248c95fc17241089acb68bcba1db07df10c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Layott","id":90828865,"login":"Layott","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODI4ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/114e75ec9c9d5651509136e204bae98f582ee87f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T10:14:23Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T10:14:23Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"message":"Give a live broadcast its own controls, and sound\n\nrequiresLinearPlayback was not enough. It takes the skip buttons away and\nstops the bar responding to a drag, but ExoPlayer still draws the bar, pinned\nfull width at the live edge, which is what it means and what nobody reads it\nas. A control that cannot be operated should not be on screen, so live now\nswaps the platform''s control bar for the three controls a broadcast actually\nhas: play, sound, and size. A recording keeps the platform''s controls, because\nscrubbing a recording is the point.\n\nSound is on by default. A browser will not autoplay with audio, so the web\nplayer has to start muted and offer a way back; a phone has no such rule, and\nthat inherited default had every screen in the app playing silently with no\nway to undo it, since ExoPlayer''s bar has no volume button.\n\nFullscreen hands the platform its chrome back, because it runs in a separate\nActivity our overlay cannot reach and the viewer would otherwise land there\nwith no visible way out. Enabling the chrome and opening fullscreen cannot\nhappen in the same tick, so the prop reaches the native side first and an\neffect opens it after that commit.\n\nPlay and mute state is mirrored off the player''s own events rather than\nassumed from our buttons: a notification, a headset button, or the fullscreen\ncontrols all move it behind our back.\n\nTypecheck is clean and the web variant is untouched. The behaviour itself is\nplatform-player behaviour and cannot be verified anywhere but a device, so it\nneeds a walk on the next APK.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JEPvbznPoLupeJmcBrdvod","tree":{"sha":"e84d4746d096717367c36c86c7ce4fbefb8899e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/trees/e84d4746d096717367c36c86c7ce4fbefb8899e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/commits/114e75ec9c9d5651509136e204bae98f582ee87f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Layott","id":90828865,"login":"Layott","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODI4ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/114e75ec9c9d5651509136e204bae98f582ee87f","node_id":"C_kwDOSVUfFtoAKDExNGU3NWVjOWM5ZDU2NTE1MDkxMzZlMjA0YmFlOThmNTgyZWU4N2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/7a9990a8cf5a8f235530682791aba551d3c36c27","sha":"7a9990a8cf5a8f235530682791aba551d3c36c27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/7a9990a8cf5a8f235530682791aba551d3c36c27"}],"sha":"114e75ec9c9d5651509136e204bae98f582ee87f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/114e75ec9c9d5651509136e204bae98f582ee87f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Layott","id":90828865,"login":"Layott","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODI4ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/7a9990a8cf5a8f235530682791aba551d3c36c27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T10:14:23Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T10:14:23Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"message":"Let somebody change their email in the app\n\nThe field was read-only under the words \"Contact support to change your\nemail\", on a platform with no support desk. Better-Auth''s changeEmail is\nenabled and the website has used it since the settings rebuild, so the app now\nhas the same form rather than a dead end.\n\nThe copy says what actually happens: the confirmation link goes to the address\ncurrently on the account, not the new one, and nothing changes until it is\nopened. A plain \"Saved\" would be wrong twice over.\n\nErrors carry the server''s own sentence now. ApiError took only a status, so\nevery failed call surfaced as \"API 400\" no matter what the route said, and\nsomebody who typed an address that is already taken learned nothing. Our\nroutes answer { error }, Better-Auth answers { message }; either is used when\nit is short enough for a toast, and anything longer is dropped rather than\ntruncated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JEPvbznPoLupeJmcBrdvod","tree":{"sha":"1c1db82074fd2e51ac6d287789940f9d594cbc7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/trees/1c1db82074fd2e51ac6d287789940f9d594cbc7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/commits/7a9990a8cf5a8f235530682791aba551d3c36c27","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Layott","id":90828865,"login":"Layott","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODI4ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/7a9990a8cf5a8f235530682791aba551d3c36c27","node_id":"C_kwDOSVUfFtoAKDdhOTk5MGE4Y2Y1YThmMjM1NTMwNjgyNzkxYWJhNTUxZDNjMzZjMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/bb7e0c7cc348a3bf26de8eb95d04e71135978e39","sha":"bb7e0c7cc348a3bf26de8eb95d04e71135978e39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/bb7e0c7cc348a3bf26de8eb95d04e71135978e39"}],"sha":"7a9990a8cf5a8f235530682791aba551d3c36c27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/7a9990a8cf5a8f235530682791aba551d3c36c27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Layott","id":90828865,"login":"Layott","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODI4ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/a3ba60220e37f120d3839d1e4bf966b07d813123/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:32:19Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:32:19Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"message":"Close the count leaks the shared type could not reach\n\nFour screens still showed audience numbers after the last pass: the channel\npage, the public profile''s clips and VODs, and the home main-channel card.\n\nThey survived because each declared its own count type in lib/api rather than\nusing the shared one in lib/types.ts, so making the shared fields optional left\nthese alone and the compiler had nothing to complain about. A clean typecheck\nwas not evidence of a clean sweep. Found by grepping for the non-optional\ndeclarations instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JxTdydZSn8tQ2knfLbya4N","tree":{"sha":"4d2faadacd45e2591236d1c2c2a97ab4a2814b65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/trees/4d2faadacd45e2591236d1c2c2a97ab4a2814b65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/commits/a3ba60220e37f120d3839d1e4bf966b07d813123","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Layott","id":90828865,"login":"Layott","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODI4ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/a3ba60220e37f120d3839d1e4bf966b07d813123","node_id":"C_kwDOSVUfFtoAKGEzYmE2MDIyMGUzN2YxMjBkMzgzOWQxZTRiZjk2NmIwN2Q4MTMxMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/0086f6337a80cf278f188c501b8d5b0678f238b0","sha":"0086f6337a80cf278f188c501b8d5b0678f238b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/0086f6337a80cf278f188c501b8d5b0678f238b0"}],"sha":"a3ba60220e37f120d3839d1e4bf966b07d813123","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/a3ba60220e37f120d3839d1e4bf966b07d813123"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Layott","id":90828865,"login":"Layott","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODI4ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/0086f6337a80cf278f188c501b8d5b0678f238b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:07:53Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T15:07:53Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"message":"Stop showing viewers how many people are watching\n\nThe other half of the backend change: audience numbers are staff only, so the\nAPI no longer sends viewerCount or viewCount to anyone but an admin.\n\nMaking the two fields optional in lib/types.ts turned the compiler into the\nchecklist. Nineteen call sites, each now rendering nothing rather than a zero,\nbecause a badge reading \"0\" where a number used to be is worse than no badge:\nit says the broadcast is empty rather than that the figure is not yours.\n\nAdmin screens read the same fields and still get real numbers, so those take\n?? 0 for narrowing rather than a behaviour change.\n\nThe stream screen keeps its 30s refetch. It was there for the count, but it is\nalso how the screen notices a broadcast ending, which still matters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JxTdydZSn8tQ2knfLbya4N","tree":{"sha":"e5a38b19b63cd6ad1b684261ff79016a78ac14be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/trees/e5a38b19b63cd6ad1b684261ff79016a78ac14be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/commits/0086f6337a80cf278f188c501b8d5b0678f238b0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Layott","id":90828865,"login":"Layott","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODI4ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/La