rred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/bb7e0c7cc348a3bf26de8eb95d04e71135978e39","node_id":"C_kwDOSVUfFtoAKGJiN2UwYzdjYzM0OGEzYmYyNmRlOGViOTVkMDRlNzExMzU5NzhlMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/cccc9d17b410277d2a873ac73bfe123b08e27f8e","sha":"cccc9d17b410277d2a873ac73bfe123b08e27f8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/cccc9d17b410277d2a873ac73bfe123b08e27f8e"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Layott/evotv-app/commit/e99472ff029af92e83e2575a1b8732db4e47dbde","sha":"e99472ff029af92e83e2575a1b8732db4e47dbde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/e99472ff029af92e83e2575a1b8732db4e47dbde"}],"sha":"bb7e0c7cc348a3bf26de8eb95d04e71135978e39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/bb7e0c7cc348a3bf26de8eb95d04e71135978e39"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Layott","id":90828865,"login":"Layott","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODI4ODY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Layott","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/e99472ff029af92e83e2575a1b8732db4e47dbde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:50:08Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:50:08Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"message":"Stop the app offering a scrub bar on a live broadcast\n\nThe website''s live player dropped its scrub bar and skip buttons, and the app\nkept both. Same reasoning applies: every second scrubbed back on a live stream\nis latency the viewer gains nothing from, and landing near the live edge\nre-buffers on arrival.\n\nThe reason it survived is that these controls are not ours. On native the player\nis the platform''s, so not rendering a scrub bar is not an option; the platform\nhas to be told not to offer one. `requiresLinearPlayback` removes skipping on\nboth iOS and Android, and `showsTimecodes` hides the position readout on iOS,\nwhere a clock against a stream with no beginning means nothing.\n\nOnly the stream screen passes `isLive`. Episodes and VODs are recordings and\nkeep seeking, which is the whole point of the flag being a flag.\n\nThe web variant is deliberately unchanged. `controls` on a `<video>` is all or\nnothing: there is no way to keep play, volume and fullscreen while dropping the\nseek bar, and `controlsList` has no \"noseek\". Turning it off would leave that\ntarget with no way to pause, which is a worse outcome than a scrub bar nobody\nneeds. The real web player is the Next app''s, which draws its own controls and\nalready removes seeking on live.\n\nNot verified on a device. It is a platform-player behaviour, so it needs a build\nto see.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014GkRDBJorYUURn4bkNe7JW","tree":{"sha":"b4ce9c774413afe4c85935cfeb40d88930734e49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/trees/b4ce9c774413afe4c85935cfeb40d88930734e49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/re