mments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/commits/cfa7bb32abce44c0050a5c8182d999f13f4b0265/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T01:26:03Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T01:26:03Z","email":"ladilawalt@gmail.com","name":"ladilawalt"},"message":"Make the admin Sections button actually open the sheet\n\nPressing Sections on any admin screen did nothing. The code read as correct,\nwhich is why it survived: the button set state and the sheet was rendered right\nbeside it.\n\nThe problem is where \"beside it\" was. The button is mounted through\n`headerRight`, which renders into the native stack header, and that header is a\nreal platform view rather than a React Native one. A full-screen `Modal` cannot\nmount inside it, so the sheet was created and never appeared. Nothing throws and\nnothing logs; the control simply looks dead.\n\nThe two now live apart. The button stays in the header, the sheet renders as a\nsibling of the navigator where a Modal has an ordinary view to mount into, and a\nsmall context carries the single piece of state between them.\n\nNot verified on a device: this needs a build to test, and the behaviour it fixes\nonly exists on native. The web target renders Modal as a DOM node and was never\naffected, so testing there would prove nothing about the case that was broken.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014GkRDBJorYUURn4bkNe7JW","tree":{"sha":"d16f280929f6d52a0eae02a790e4e405cc5740f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/trees/d16f280929f6d52a0eae02a790e4e405cc5740f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Layott/evotv-app/git/commits/cfa7bb32abce44c0050a5c8182d999f13f4b0265","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90828865?v=4","even